  <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
    <name>EDM activeXTextClass</name>
    <text>1. Start with piezo disabled.

2. Set bias voltage to 25 V.

3. Set piezo to Manual mode. Enable piezo.

4. Adjust steppers to zero detune frequency.

5. Set piezo to Feedback mode. Firmware will then
continuously adjust piezo as needed to zero detune 
frequency.</text>
    <x>492</x>
    <y>492</y>
    <width>277</width>
    <height>182</height>
    <font>
      <font family="Liberation Sans" style="REGULAR" size="12.0">
      </font>
    </font>
    <foreground_color>
      <color name="black-14" red="0" green="0" blue="0">
      </color>
    </foreground_color>
    <background_color>
      <color name="Disconn/Invalid" red="255" green="255" blue="255">
      </color>
    </background_color>
    <auto_size>true</auto_size>
  </widget>
  <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
    <name>EDM activeXTextClass</name>
    <text>Notes:

-DC Offset is used only in Manual mode. It is added to the 
Bias voltage. Its value is overwritten during switch from
Feedback to Manual mode. 

-Feedback Setpoint can be used to compensate for an 
observed fixed frequency offset.

-Bias is used to operate the piezo awayfrom the limit 
of its operating range. It changes rarely or never.

-The piezo range is set to: Bias-25V to Bias+25V</text>
    <x>840</x>
    <y>476</y>
    <width>311</width>
    <height>215</height>
    <font>
      <font family="Liberation Sans" style="REGULAR" size="12.0">
      </font>
    </font>
    <foreground_color>
      <color name="black-14" red="0" green="0" blue="0">
      </color>
    </foreground_color>
    <background_color>
      <color name="Disconn/Invalid" red="255" green="255" blue="255">
      </color>
    </background_color>
    <auto_size>true</auto_size>
  </widget>
